    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`vllm serve --config cfg.yaml` turns a YAML list item that is a mapping into a Python repr (`{'name': ...}`) instead of JSON. As a result, JSON-valued list arguments such as `--lora-modules` cannot be written as YAML mappings and fail with `Invalid JSON format for --lora-modules`. This PR serializes those items with `json.dumps`, the same way top-level mapping values are already handled.\n\nRelated: #9655 (closed as not planned; it covered YAML LoRA lists before list support existed). #23528 added support for lists of strings, but mappings inside lists were never handled.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The YAML config below now loads two `LoRAModulePath` entries. Before this change, startup failed with `serve: error: Invalid JSON format for --lora-modules: {'base_model_name': ..., 'name': ..., 'path': ...}`.\n\n  ```yaml\n  lora-modules:\n    - sql-lora=jeeejeee/llama32-3b-text2sql-spider\n    - name: sql-lora-2\n      path: jeeejeee/llama32-3b-text2sql-spider\n      base_model_name: meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct\n  ```\n- Scalar list items (`- item`, `name=path`) are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nI added a regression test, `test_lora_modules_from_yaml_config`, to `tests/entrypoints/common/test_cli_args.py`. It goes through the real `vllm` → `serve` parser built by `make_arg_parser` with `--config`.\n\nBefore the fix (fix reverted, test kept):\n\n```text\n$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/entrypoints/common/test_cli_args.py::test_lora_modules_from_yaml_config -q\n__main__.py serve: error: Invalid JSON format for --lora-modules: {'base_model_name': 'llama', 'name': 'module2', 'path': '/path/to/module2'}\n1 failed in 2.23s\n```\n\nAfter the fix:\n\n```text\n$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/entrypoints/common/test_cli_args.py::test_lora_modules_from_yaml_config -q\n1 passed in 1.73s\n\n$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/entrypoints/common/test_cli_args.py tests/utils_/test_argparse_utils.py -q\n102 passed in 16.04s\n```\n\nI also parsed the docs example above through the real serve parser. It produced `[LoRAModulePath(name='sql-lora', ...), LoRAModulePath(name='sql-lora-2', ..., base_model_name='meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct')]`.\n\n`pre-commit run --files <changed files>` passes: ruff, mypy, typos, markdownlint, and the Buildkite key and test-tethering checks.\n\nNo model evaluation was run. This change only affects CLI argument parsing and does not touch model execution or outputs.\n\n## Details\n\n**Root cause:** in `FlexibleArgumentParser.load_config_file`, the `list` branch emitted `str(item)` for each item. The `dict` branch just below already emits `json.dumps(value)` because CLI parsers expect JSON. A mapping inside a list therefore reached `LoRAParserAction` as a single-quoted repr containing commas, so it took the JSON branch and `json.loads` failed.\n\n**Fix:** list items that are `dict` or `list` are now emitted with `json.dumps`. Everything else still uses `str()`.\n\n**Compatibility:**\n- `load_config_file` has a single caller, `_pull_args_from_config`.\n- A mapping inside a list could never be parsed before, so no working config changes.\n- Nested lists of numbers serialize the same either way (`[1, 2]`).\n- No argument parses Python-repr list items.\n\n**CI:** the `Entrypoints Unit` step runs `tests/entrypoints/common`. I added `vllm/utils/argparse_utils.py` to its `source_file_dependencies` so that changes to the parser alone also trigger these serve `--config` tests.\n\n**Docs:** `docs/configuration/serve_args.md` now shows that lists become repeated values and nested mappings become JSON, using `--lora-modules` as the example.\n\n**Not a duplicate:** I searched open and closed PRs and issues on vllm-project/vllm for `load_config_file`, `_pull_args_from_config`, `config yaml list of dicts`, `lora-modules yaml`, `config.yaml lora_modules`, `FlexibleArgumentParser list`, and `config list items json`. The open `--config` PRs cover different bugs:\n- #49057 and #58102: YAML `false` values are dropped.\n- #43548: `--config=<path>` is ignored.\n- #51623, #52077, #60319: empty or invalid YAML files.\n- #62215, #58096: negative float values on the CLI.\n- #60329: JSON-serializes list values in `vllm bench sweep`, which is a different code path.\n\n#54216 (closed, not merged) bundled several `--config` fixes but did not touch list items. No open PR changes the list-item serialization in `load_config_file`.\n\n**AI assistance:** I wrote this change with AI assistance (Cursor Agent). I have reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
